{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And no man shall come up with you</b> — that the elders of Israel should not come up with you at all, as they did with the first tablets (Exodus 24:1)." "<b>And also no man shall be seen throughout the entire mountain</b> — even at the foot of the mountain, the place where Israel stood the first time (Exodus 19:17)." "<b>Also the sheep and the cattle, let them not graze opposite that mountain</b> — מנגד (opposite). For the first time they were only warned not to touch it, whether beast or man (Exodus 19:13). Now, that earlier warning was still in effect, for the Glory was always on the mountain until the [latter] tablets were given; but now He was stricter at the time of the giving of these tablets than at the first stationing. And the reason for all this is that the first event was for the sake of all Israel, whereas this was for Moses alone, by his merit and through his prayer, and the Glory revealed on the latter mountain would be greater than on the first."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {2 "The Hebrew text contains a bracketed correction: (הראשונות) [האחרונות], i.e., the first tablets crossed out and replaced with the latter tablets. I have adopted the corrected reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:32.927717096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}